      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal|Guarded Write Journal]] page describes a mechanism used by the guarded tool executor to journal file operations for rollback on failure. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core function**: Before overwriting any file, the system records the file\u0027s prior state (its previous content, or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist) into an in-memory write journal.\n\n**Rollback capability**: If an agent run fails\u2014due to hitting a turn cap, encountering an unrecoverable error, or having all writes denied\u2014the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed and deleting newly created files.\n\n**All-or-nothing semantics**: This approach provides atomic transaction-like behavior for writes without requiring a database transaction. The journal itself acts as a transaction log, held in the process\u0027s memory for the duration of a single run.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never uses the journal\u0027s rollback functionality, since it has no write capability at all.",
